Package: underwood
Version: 2.6.4
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8)
Recommends: hunspell, hunspell-es, hunspell-en-us, xterm, fonts-dejavu-core
Suggests: libreoffice-writer
Maintainer: Silvestre Parbut
Homepage: https://github.com/SilvestreParbut/Underwood
Description: Terminal-based word processor
 Underwood is a minimalist word processor for the terminal, designed for creative writing: novels, short stories, essays, and screenplays.
 .
 It includes formatting (bold, italics, underline), three heading levels with a chapter map, spell-checking via Hunspell, search and replace, and export options for RTF, .MD, TXT, DOCX, and PDF.
 .
 It works with a mouse, or—if none is available—entirely via keyboard: selection using Shift+arrow keys and menus via F9.
